   "body": "## Goal\nGive a separate, pinned semantic review of the authored example package `wp1-examples-0121-v1` (task #584, iteration 0121) under `benchmark/writing/`. Report, do not fix: you have no repository write paths and must not propose edits as done. The author of the package was exposed to all prior analysis; the gain of this task is a verdict from a session that first derives its own expectation from the sources and only then opens the package. Expected gain and its check: the next shaper reads in `.session/report.md` one verdict line per dimension (Standards CLEAR/NOT-CLEAR; Spec CLEAR/NOT-CLEAR), a per-ID agreement table for the five relation IDs in both examples, and a plain statement whether the package is adequate evidence for a later, separate key revision to consider releasing the F4 block. This task does NOT release F4, promotes nothing and clears no readiness gap. No session can run LabVIEW: claim no native validity, behaviour, build, dependency resolution or save-version preservation, and treat any such claim in the package as a finding.\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] FIRST, before opening any file listed under \"Later reads\" in Budget: record observed HEAD and tree, then derive your own cold expectation from the sources only (`benchmark/real-project-0107/original.lvproj`, `benchmark/real-project-0107/LICENSE.txt`, `benchmark/writing/method.json` task 4 and common answer rule, `benchmark/protocol.md` answer/grading/preservation clauses). It contains at least: the WP1 change locator (byte offset, line, old and new byte), the expected output size and SHA256 computed by you, the preservation ID list read from method.json, the list of URL references the project XML declares with their line locators, and what a complete pre/post inventory and original/output map must contain according to those sources. Save it as `.session/artifacts/wp1-examples-cold-0122.json` with a note of which files had been opened at that point. If you opened a later-read file earli