se changed leaves, old/new source pins, new-file sizes/SHA256, actual verification command/exit/summary and all remaining prerequisites. Include a compact reviewer handoff naming the candidate HEAD/tree and exact new and unchanged files, so a separate session can review only this changed scope. Do not claim independence or repeat the cold derivation; preserve #587's disclosure of startup ordering/model continuity limits. No preparation index, method/protocol, proposal, original project, license or product edits; no arms or native execution.\n## Verification\npython3 -I benchmark/writing/check_wp1_key_0123.py\n## Context\n- `benchmark/writing/wp1-examples-0121.md`, especially What next: the shaper read this whole; the model is explicitly conditional, all declared dependencies absent, historical maps blocked.\n- Review #587 (iteration 0122) reports Standards CLEAR / Spec CLEAR at HEAD 650c282024d073a59710cdb0b2cfe5463f9b4a9d, tree 752cb3a6b4010e6af388a1445402679aa564830d. It found the package adequate for a later key revision for the new conditional examples, not readiness. It reports no Later-read exposure before saving its expectation, but startup ordering/protocol-read deviations and uncertified model continuity. The preserved input is the detailed authority; do not rerun completed probes.\n- Source pins carried from the prior memory and confirmed by #587, not newly measured by this shaper: wp1-key-0119.json 2afdca4bfc6feaa9464348bed7709b0657ea1ccbbe5d6b0a33b549c78f41c142; method.json 276f2881c70eae311195a4cc0a802e316ca06a206a0f1d16e7f041205fd3b0ac; benchmark/protocol.md 1aeb83227dc11761160ff80d24eb03a216a2531d90c1a6d10ccb25bb85c7eb2f; original.lvproj 1d5e140df788ce1f91c89241bbdb1227c5e4cc6fdf6efbbd820974bbe6082dcf; LICENSE.txt 529e65e6fc185d39380efd3957ef1c9acd0aac31ed288bcb9d124840861f03a2.\n- Package SHA256 reported by its author and confirmed by #587: wp1-examples-0121.json 8c6f6d82e4fdc9db268827fd1cc942daebf84319336bba3e7141a7a110a8e382; .md b450a9d0b2d5abe9c72a7f16514705b2f72a8c4d835131843f59c2b17c3e0120; check_wp1_examples_0121.py 2050ffc23448503f96ea1b5a5769f47260cb67ca478c38f2967e9276d3cf46c1; wp1-examples-0121-verification.json d7a0bc9caab9e32a265f5645ecb3dbe47c5b05146078ffb63af9f7c667e0bcd3; wp1-examples-0121-pre-edit.md 649b71383e6f0467d41e97db38a3cb660a75d9e631abc411295b05fa0e35fa4b.\n- docs/perpetua/evaluation.md: oracle, actual isolation, matched comparison and owner acceptance remain requirements. This task addresses only operative key incorporation of the reviewed conditional controls. C1 human adjudication is not solved by a checker.\n## Budget\nRead whole: `benchmark/writing/wp1-examples-0121.md`, `benchmark/writing/wp1-key-0119.md`, `benchmark/real-project-0107/original.lvproj`, `benchmark/real-project-0107/LICENSE.txt`, the two staged 587 JSON inputs (bounded queried output preferred), `docs/perpetua/evaluation.md`. Read before edits: `benchmark/writing/wp1-key-0119.json` by focused query of identity, affected WP1 operative leaves, F4 and example slots; `benchmark/writing/method.json` common answer rule and WP1 task; `benchmark/protocol.md` grading/preservation clauses. Later as needed: `benchmark/writing/wp1-examples-0121.json` by query, its checker and verification/pre-edit record; `benchmark/writing/wp1-disposition-review-0120.json` identity and F4 containment only. Never dump base64 or whole large JSON. Keep command output short; save identity/pin evidence and draft the key early. Do not read global gap maps, POC files, sources.json or old session histories; do not replay #574/#581/#587 review probes, any cold derivation, historical checkers/builders or preserved audit. No git commit, shell expansion, pipes or redirection. Engine verification cannot read session artifacts/inputs. If unfinished, save work and name the missing check; do not redo the preserved review."
